WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.467
-Welcome, everybody.
Welcome, welcome, welcome to

00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:03.701
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.701 --> 00:00:05.501
You're here. You made it.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:07.501
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:00:07.501 --> 00:00:08.968
Guys, I'm so excited
about this --

00:00:08.968 --> 00:00:11.400
Shawn Mendes is here
and he is my --

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:15.100
[ Cheering and applause ]
[ Rimshot ]

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:17.133
He is my cohost tonight.

00:00:17.133 --> 00:00:20.300
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.067
That's right,
Shawn Mendes is here

00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:24.334
and like you've never
seen him before --

00:00:24.334 --> 00:00:25.634
with sleeves.

00:00:25.634 --> 00:00:26.334
-Oh.
-Yes.

00:00:26.334 --> 00:00:28.167
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:30.601
Do you guys know
that Shawn was born in Canada?

00:00:30.601 --> 00:00:31.934
-Yes!
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:31.934 --> 00:00:33.033
-Now I'm trying to figure out,

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.067
did he really want to be here

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:35.534
or was he just too polite
to say no?

00:00:35.534 --> 00:00:36.734
[ Laughter ]
I don't know.

00:00:36.734 --> 00:00:39.200
Let's get to some news.
I read that Amazon stock

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.200
just crashed
after the company reported

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:43.667
a loss of nearly $4 billion.

00:00:43.667 --> 00:00:45.801
-Wow.
-Yeah, Amazon stock is crashing.

00:00:45.801 --> 00:00:47.267
Netflix stock is crashing.

00:00:47.267 --> 00:00:48.968
Right now, everyone
who invested in Beanie Babies

00:00:48.968 --> 00:00:51.167
is like, "Well, well, well,
who's the financial

00:00:51.167 --> 00:00:53.934
[ Laughter and applause ]
genius now?"

00:00:53.934 --> 00:00:56.400
But this should help business --
once the bad news broke,

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.567
Amazon executives spent
the night getting drunk

00:00:58.567 --> 00:01:00.701
and ordering stuff
off of Amazon, so there you go.

00:01:00.701 --> 00:01:02.834
[ Cheering and applause ]
Go right back up.

00:01:02.834 --> 00:01:04.667
Right now,
Jeff Bezos is so stressed,

00:01:04.667 --> 00:01:06.501
his hair grew in
and then fell out again.

00:01:06.501 --> 00:01:08.234
It's just unbelievable.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:09.801
Yeah, it's a tough day for Bezos

00:01:09.801 --> 00:01:12.834
because his net worth shrunk
by $13 billion.

00:01:12.834 --> 00:01:14.934
[ Awws ]

00:01:14.934 --> 00:01:16.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.167 --> 00:01:18.334
We'll be sending around
a basket for collections.

00:01:18.334 --> 00:01:20.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.033 --> 00:01:22.400
Yeah, his network shrunk
by $13 billion

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:23.901
and, due to cold weather,

00:01:23.901 --> 00:01:25.267
his rocket shrunk three inches.

00:01:25.267 --> 00:01:26.467
It's terrible.
-Whoa!

00:01:26.467 --> 00:01:28.968
[ Laughter and oohs ]
-Worse.
-Whoa!

00:01:28.968 --> 00:01:31.234
Oh! Oh!

00:01:31.234 --> 00:01:33.267
Some more business news --
I saw that, last year,

00:01:33.267 --> 00:01:36.634
Subway closed more
than 1,000 locations in the U.S.

00:01:36.634 --> 00:01:37.634
[ Awws ]

00:01:37.634 --> 00:01:38.934
One thousand stores is a lot.

00:01:38.934 --> 00:01:41.400
That's over 50,000 footlongs
of retail space.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:44.934
It's kind of annoying
because the stores are gone,

00:01:44.934 --> 00:01:47.667
but the smell of nine-grain
honey oat bread still remains.

00:01:47.667 --> 00:01:49.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:50.701
Well, get this --
Snapple announced

00:01:50.701 --> 00:01:53.601
that it's going to rebrand
its diet Snapple drinks

00:01:53.601 --> 00:01:56.100
as Snapple Zero Sugar.

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:57.467
But don't worry.
It'll still taste like

00:01:57.467 --> 00:01:58.667
the drink you've never tried.

00:01:58.667 --> 00:02:01.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.367 --> 00:02:05.400
Diet -- No, I'm going to get
the Peach.

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:07.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.167 --> 00:02:08.767
Some entertainment news --

00:02:08.767 --> 00:02:10.434
Tom Cruise has revealed
that the title

00:02:10.434 --> 00:02:12.767
of "Mission: Impossible 7"
will be

00:02:12.767 --> 00:02:16.100
"Mission: Impossible --
Dead Reckoning Part One."

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:17.534
[ Oohs ]

00:02:17.534 --> 00:02:19.200
So far,
the impossible mission is

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:20.968
fitting that entire title
on a marquee.

00:02:20.968 --> 00:02:22.434
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.434 --> 00:02:24.467
Yeah, that's a long title.
Right now, our movie titles

00:02:24.467 --> 00:02:26.567
are starting to look like
the poster for Coachella.

00:02:26.567 --> 00:02:29.000
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.100
Oh, my --

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:32.133
[ Cacophony of cheering
and applause ]

00:02:32.133 --> 00:02:36.534
[ Rimshot ]

00:02:43.734 --> 00:02:45.200
This is --

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:46.267
[ Laughs ]

00:02:46.267 --> 00:02:48.334
Wow!
Shawn Mendes, everybody.

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:50.901
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:02:50.901 --> 00:02:52.234
Oh, my goodness.

00:02:52.234 --> 00:02:54.801
Wow! Wow!
Shawn Mendes,

00:02:54.801 --> 00:02:58.234
you're young, you're talented,

00:02:58.234 --> 00:03:00.434
you're good-looking.

00:03:00.434 --> 00:03:02.133
It is like --

00:03:02.133 --> 00:03:03.567
It's like looking into a mirror.

00:03:03.567 --> 00:03:05.000
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:06.701
-I feel differently.
-Yeah.

00:03:06.701 --> 00:03:08.534
[ Laughter ]
Hey, you want to try
some monologue jokes?

00:03:08.534 --> 00:03:09.834
-Yeah, sure.
Let's do it, guys.

00:03:09.834 --> 00:03:11.400
Well, I heard that, this year,
New York City is getting

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.334
60 new electric buses.

00:03:13.334 --> 00:03:15.133
-Yeah, electric buses.

00:03:15.133 --> 00:03:16.167
Or, as they're also known,

00:03:16.167 --> 00:03:17.200
subways.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:18.667
[ Laughter ]
How about this one?

00:03:18.667 --> 00:03:20.367
Try this one.
-Yeah, hey, I saw
that a new poll said

00:03:20.367 --> 00:03:22.133
that every average American

00:03:22.133 --> 00:03:24.501
sets four different alarms
to wake up in the morning.

00:03:24.501 --> 00:03:25.934
Did you know that?
-Yeah. No, I didn't know.

00:03:25.934 --> 00:03:28.300
The poll also found that the
average person's spouse says,

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:30.234
"If that goes off a fifth time,
we're getting a divorce."

00:03:30.234 --> 00:03:32.334
[ Laughter ]
-Yep. Four alarms.
Everyone's like,

00:03:32.334 --> 00:03:34.100
"We don't know why
we're so tired,"

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:36.734
when they went back scrolling
TikTok 'til 3:00 am.

00:03:36.734 --> 00:03:37.901
Yeah, of course.
That's what we all do.

00:03:37.901 --> 00:03:39.501
[ Laughter and applause ]
Listen to this --

00:03:39.501 --> 00:03:41.000
a professional soccer player
in England

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:42.400
is missing a game tomorrow

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:45.300
because he got a cotton swab
stuck in his ear.

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:46.067
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.067 --> 00:03:47.067
-Johnson &amp; Johnson's like,

00:03:47.067 --> 00:03:48.634
"Can we have one good day

00:03:48.634 --> 00:03:50.667
of PR?
-"Please."

00:03:50.667 --> 00:03:53.934
-Just one?" I mean,
he could remove the Q-Tip,

00:03:53.934 --> 00:03:54.968
but he's not allowed.

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:55.634
No hands.

00:03:55.634 --> 00:03:56.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.434 --> 00:03:57.434
-Yeah, you're right, yeah.

00:03:57.434 --> 00:03:58.734
No one knows what to do

00:03:58.734 --> 00:04:00.100
because it's the first time

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:01.934
a soccer player has had
an injury that's real.

00:04:01.934 --> 00:04:04.901
[ Laughter and oohs ]
Oh, stop it.

00:04:04.901 --> 00:04:06.334
Hey! Oh, hey!

00:04:06.334 --> 00:04:08.234
[ Cymbals crash ]
Shawn Mendes is here.
Don't do this!

00:04:08.234 --> 00:04:10.367
Don't do this to me
in front of Shawn Mendes.

00:04:10.367 --> 00:04:12.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.501 --> 00:04:13.601
We had a deal.

00:04:13.601 --> 00:04:14.667
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.667 --> 00:04:15.868
Finally, a high school teacher

00:04:15.868 --> 00:04:17.234
in California was arrested

00:04:17.234 --> 00:04:19.834
after she was allegedly
caught drunk in the classroom.

00:04:19.834 --> 00:04:23.033
-Yeah. Drunk while teaching,
or, as parents call that,

00:04:23.033 --> 00:04:24.734
homeschooling.
-That's correct.

00:04:24.734 --> 00:04:27.133
[ Cheering and applause ]
We have a great show tonight.

